// 40MHz crystal intended as the ESP32-S3 main crystal (and for other 40MHz
// MCUs). Hosonic E1SB series: 2.0 x 1.6mm seam-sealed four-terminal package
// (hosonic-e1sb.pdf p. 1), on FP_Crystal_SMD_2016_4Pin_E1SB, the sheet's
// recommended land (crystal_48mhz.cohdl). Pins 1 and 3 are the crystal
// electrodes; pins 2 and 4 are connected to the lid.
//
// MPN UNVERIFIED: E1SB40E001G00E is patterned on the 48MHz part's
// E1SB48E001G00E. The E1SB sheet is a series sheet with no ordering-code
// key, so it does not establish that this MPN exists, nor its load
// capacitance, tolerance or stability. Series limits at 40MHz: CL 6-16pF
// "or specify", +/-10ppm at 25C, +/-15ppm over temperature, ESR <= 60ohm.
// Confirm the exact part with Hosonic or a distributor before fitting.
//
// Load capacitors: the "10pF load class" and "C1=C4 10pF + 24nH series
// inductor on XTAL_N, trimmed by measurement" guidance previously given
// here comes from Espressif's ESP32-S3 hardware design guidelines, which
// are not pinned in this repo, so it is not source-checked. The E1SB sheet
// gives no external-component values; size the caps from the confirmed
// part's CL.
//
// Orientation: the sheet defines no index mark. Its drawings show the pin-2
// terminal (a ground) with a cut inner corner; the footprint's pin-1 dot
// marks pad 1, not that corner. A 90 degree rotation puts the crystal
// electrodes on the ground pads (180 degrees is harmless).

#[doc("docs/hosonic-e1sb.pdf")]
pub device Crystal40MHz {
    pins {
        required XIN: 1 [passive]
        required GND: 2, 4 [passive]
        required XOUT: 3 [passive]
    }
}
impl Crystal for Crystal40MHz {}

#[doc("docs/hosonic-e1sb.pdf")]
pub part XTAL_40MHZ: Crystal40MHz {
    primary { mfr: "Hosonic", mpn: "E1SB40E001G00E", footprint: FP_Crystal_SMD_2016_4Pin_E1SB }
}
